Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.32,0:00:04.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Use two dials as a map:\N{\c&H3468EB&}quadrupole{\c&HF7F4F2&} across, dipole up.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.16,0:00:08.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}With the knob low, the state\Ncircles in one whirlpool, and stays.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.86,0:00:12.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}A mirror twin circles the\Nmirror whirlpool: dipole down.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.92,0:00:16.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Each start is trapped.\NThe dipole never changes sign.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.66,0:00:18.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Now turn {\c&H7AAF1B&}Gamma{\c&HF7F4F2&} up.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.96,0:00:24.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Just above zero point eight six, the\Nwhirlpools touch: a narrow corridor opens.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.65,0:00:29.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The state lingers on one side,\Nthen slips through. The {\c&H3468EB&}dipole{\c&HF7F4F2&} flips.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.55,0:00:34.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Nothing here is random. So,\Nwill the flips come like clockwork?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.50,0:00:40.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}No. Long waits and\Nshort ones, irregularly.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.27,0:00:44.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The dipole's sign prints uneven\Nstripes, like the seafloor.
